While I understand why you can only run one ring per hand, I've always 
thought that if you were polymorphed into a marilith (a five armed
monster), you should be able to wear five rings.  Instead of asking
you which ring finger you wanted to use (rl), it would ask which ring 
finger (1-5).

I've also thought that they should be able to weild 5 different weapons,
or a two-handed weapon and three others, or two two-handed weapons and
one other.  Or (I guess) use four arms for weapons, and one for a 
sheild.  They already get five weapon attacks -- why not five different
ones?  (Imagine weilding Stormbringer and the Tsurgi, and a sheild of
reflection.  Or Frostbrand, Firebrand, Grayswandir, Mjollnir, and 
Excalibur.)

The current strategy of giving the marilith 5 weapon attacks with
one weapon doesn't really make sense.  It makes them sound like just
a fast monster, not a five armed one.  Also, why do they get five 
attacks even if they're wearing a sheild (I know, it's because it's
a lot easier to code them that way).

This also begs the question of why humans can't weild two weapons with
two hands (instead of one and a sheild).  I guess you could argue that
characters are all decidedly right-handed, and too clumsy with their
left hands to do anything but hold a sheild.  
